  "body": "<h2>In the Rhythm of the River</h2><p>The Pieniny are mountains that do not overwhelm with size but delight with form. It is here that nature created one of the most spectacular river gorges in Europe.</p><p>A raft trip down the Dunajec is a journey through time. As the raftsmen tell legends and limestone walls rise high above the water, you can feel the rhythm of life that has not changed for generations. It is a lesson in humility before the river that has been carving this landscape for centuries.</p><h2>Summits Within Reach</h2><p>Slow travel in the Pieniny is above all about mindfulness. It is climbing Trzy Korony at sunrise, when the first rays illuminate the valley and awaken the forests, and the air is crystal clear.</p><p>It is worth taking time to walk through Szczawnica, discovering its spa charm, drinking mineral waters, and watching how life slowly unfolds in a resort that has remained an oasis of calm for seekers of regeneration for years.</p>",
